      'subtitle' => 'Role-based training, practical assessment and verifiable certification for hotel teams, from Altus Advisory in Riyadh. In Arabic, English and the languages your staff speak.',
      'body' => '<h2>What is Hospitality Academy?</h2><p>Hospitality Academy is the public training academy of Altus Advisory, a hospitality and business strategy firm based in Riyadh, Saudi Arabia. It runs on the altus Hospitality Knowledge &amp; Performance platform, which delivers hotel staff training by job role and then checks whether each person can actually do the work.</p><h2>How is it different from an ordinary online course?</h2><p>Completion is not treated as proof. Each learner moves from role-based learning to theory and practical assessment, and the result is recorded against defined competencies. Where a gap appears, an action plan and a reassessment follow, so managers see evidence of capability rather than a list of finished videos.</p><ol><li>Learning assigned from the requirements of the job role</li><li>Theory assessment and a practical assessment on the same standard</li><li>A competency record, identified gaps and a corrective action plan</li><li>Reassessment, a readiness status and a verifiable certificate</li></ol><h2>Which hotel departments does the academy cover?</h2><p>The master curriculum is organised into ten core professional domains: hotel fundamentals, front office, housekeeping, food and beverage, kitchen, sales and marketing, revenue and reservations, guest experience, quality and audit, and security and safety. Browse the <a href="/en/courses">course catalogue</a> or follow a structured <a href="/en/learning-paths">learning path</a> for a specific role.</p><h2>Which languages can hotel staff learn in?</h2><p>Arabic and English are built in as one experience, with Arabic laid out right to left. The staff workspace also supports Hindi, Urdu, Filipino, Bengali, Nepali and Malayalam, so the standard is understood by the people who deliver it on every shift.</p><h2>Can an employer check a certificate?</h2><p>Yes. Every certificate carries a unique number and a verification code, and anyone can confirm whether it is valid, expired or revoked on the <a href="/en/verify">certificate verification page</a>.</p><h2>How does the academy support Vision 2030?</h2><p>Vision 2030 targets 150 million annual visits to the Kingdom by 2030 and places Saudi human capital at the centre of that growth. Altus Advisory aligns the academy with those goals through bilingual learning paths, assessed competence and certification that hotels in Saudi Arabia and the GCC can rely on.</p><p>Hotel owners and operators can <a href="/en/hotels">set up training for their properties</a> or <a href="/en/contact">speak with the academy team in Riyadh</a>.</p>',
