      'subtitle' => 'The public training academy of Altus Advisory in Riyadh: who stands behind the content, how it is approved, and what we will and will not claim.',
      'body' => '<h2>Who runs Hospitality Academy?</h2><p>Hospitality Academy is operated by Altus Advisory, a boutique strategy firm headquartered in Riyadh, Kingdom of Saudi Arabia, serving clients across the GCC and MENA. Altus works through two integrated divisions, Hospitality Solutions and Business Growth Solutions, and the academy is how its operating standards reach hotel teams directly.</p><h2>What experience is the training content based on?</h2><p>The content draws on the operating standards of the Altus founders, whose combined leadership experience exceeds 60 years, gained inside Marriott, IHG, Starwood and Accor systems and in independent hotels. Training starts from standard operating procedures as they are performed on shift, not from a generic course library.</p><h2>How does the academy relate to the altus platform?</h2><p>The academy is the public entry point to the altus Hospitality Knowledge &amp; Performance platform. Inside the platform, hotels assign learning by role, run theory and practical assessments, track competency gaps and action plans, and see each employee\'s readiness. A governed AI assistant answers staff questions only from approved content and says so when that content does not cover a question.</p><h2>How is training content approved?</h2><p>Every lesson, procedure and assessment passes a governed review before learners see it.</p><ol><li>The author prepares a draft.</li><li>The draft receives internal approval.</li><li>The draft receives quality approval.</li><li>The content is published and its version is recorded.</li></ol><p>Authors cannot approve their own work, and earlier versions remain on record so an auditor can see which standard applied on any date.</p><h2>What principles guide the academy?</h2><p>The academy follows the principles Altus Advisory applies to every mandate.</p><ul><li>Evidence over intuition: capability is shown through assessment, not assumed from attendance.</li><li>Standards that hold on every shift, in Arabic, English and the workforce languages hotel staff use.</li><li>Partnership beyond the mandate: knowledge stays inside the client organisation after the engagement ends.</li><li>Support for Saudi human capital, in line with the Vision 2030 goals for Saudization and youth empowerment.</li></ul><h2>What does the academy not claim?</h2><p>This site publishes no pass rates, client endorsements or accreditation claims. A certificate states exactly what it records: who completed which course or programme, on what date, with what result, and whether it is still valid. Read <a href="/en/certificates">how certification works</a>, or learn more about <a href="/en/altus">Altus Advisory and its services</a>.</p>',
