      'body' => '<h2>Why do hotels need proof of capability, not just course completion?</h2><p>Most hotels already know what their teams should do. The difficulty is proving that each person can do it to the current standard, and finding the gaps before a guest, an audit or an inspection does. Altus Advisory built the altus Hospitality Knowledge &amp; Performance platform to close that gap for hotels in Riyadh and across Saudi Arabia.</p><h2>What does a hotel get from the platform?</h2><p>A single workspace where training, assessment and evidence sit together for every property.</p><ul><li>Learning assigned to people, job roles, departments or cohorts, with due dates and exemptions</li><li>Theory assessments and practical assessments scored on weighted rubrics, where a critical criterion caps the result</li><li>Competency profiles, a gap heatmap, action plans with evidence upload and reassessment</li><li>A readiness status for each employee, including opening readiness for pre-opening teams</li><li>Quality audits, KPIs and reports exported to CSV and XLSX</li><li>A governed AI assistant that answers only from your approved SOPs and policies, with citations</li><li>Property branding: your logo, colours and name</li></ul><h2>Who sees what inside the platform?</h2><p>Access follows your organisation. A department head sees their team, a general manager sees the property, and an executive sees the portfolio overview and a printable board report. Every step is scoped to your organisation and recorded in an audit log, and no organisation can see another organisation\'s data.</p><h2>Which properties is the platform designed for?</h2><p>According to the Altus Advisory corporate profile, the platform is purpose-built for independent hotels, serviced apartments and SME establishments across Saudi Arabia and the Arab region that need practical, standards-based training without the cost and complexity of global-chain systems. The need is growing: Saudi Ministry of Tourism preliminary data records 122 million domestic and international visits in 2025, and Vision 2030 targets 150 million annual visits by 2030.</p><h2>How do we get started?</h2><p>Setup starts from your structure, not from an empty catalogue.</p><ol><li>Share your properties, departments and approximate headcount per department.</li><li>Altus sets up the organisation and links job roles to the competencies they require.</li><li>Mandatory training is assigned, so staff open their own list on their first login.</li><li>Managers follow completion, assessment results and readiness from their dashboard.</li></ol><p>See the <a href="/en/hotels/training">training programmes by department</a>, browse <a href="/en/programs">certification programmes</a>, or <a href="/en/contact">talk to the academy team</a>.</p>',
